No recursion-depth guard or limit exists that is missing; the actual recursive-descent BER decoder uses an explicit state machine (`asn1Spec`/`state` loop with stDecodeValue/stTryAsExplicitTag) rather than unbounded Python recursion, and the only explicit recursion-break observed (univ.py:876) is a correct anti-recursion fix in BitString.prettyPrint. No genuine resource-exhaustion (CWE-400/664) vulnerability confirmed; the heuristics are pattern-matching on identifier names only.
